   "id": 616415,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "The motivation for the Democratic-controlled Congress to overwhelmingly pass a Republican president’s plan for a national highway system in 1956 was",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1173627,
     "content_html": "fear of a nuclear attack by the Soviet Union"
    },
    {
     "id": 1173626,
     "content_html": "the dismal condition of the existing American highway system"
    },
    {
     "id": 1173628,
     "content_html": "an opportunity to create jobs and stimulate economic growth in the style of the New Deal"
    },
    {
     "id": 1173625,
     "content_html": "the support that a majority of Democrats gave President Eisenhower"
    }
   ],
